  "factor_name": "Volatility-Normalized Drawdown Duration Reversal",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "lag1(sessions_since_most_recent_rolling_high(close, 60) / annualized_volatility(close_returns, 20))",
    "description": "Ranks assets higher when they have spent more sessions since their most recent rolling 60-session high, normalized by 20-session annualized volatility. The one-session lag prevents look-ahead. It is interpreted as a contrarian reversal signal: prolonged drawdown duration has historically preceded stronger forward returns in this cross-asset universe."
